extern-vocabulary.slp:1:30: error[SL0200]: `List<i64>` cannot cross the C boundary as the parameter `values`
  |
 1 | (extern "hal_take" (hal-take (values (List i64))) -> i64)
  |                              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  = help: an `extern` parameter is an integer type, `f64`, `bool`, `(Ptr T)`, `(& String)`, `(& (Slice T))`, `(&mut (List T))`, `(&mut (Array T N))`, a `(&mut ...)` of a word-width scalar, or a `(Fn ...)` over scalars
  = note: an aggregate does not cross by value: every field is a machine word and the value is a heap block, which is not what C means by a struct
